(6) condition (I) of Prop. 6.6 with the family {B, complement of B}, Y = {0,1}, one question, fair-coin human:
  S = (1.0, 1.0): m_x(S) = 0.000, ||S||_pi = 1.000, ratio 0.000
  S = (2.0, 2.0): m_x(S) = 0.000, ||S||_pi = 2.000, ratio 0.000
  S = (1.0, -1.0): m_x(S) = 0.500, ||S||_pi = 1.000, ratio 0.500
  (the direction S = (1, 1) gives ratio 0, so (I) fails for every mu0 > 0; reachable books satisfy
   S(B) = -S(complement), and on that line the ratio is 1/2)

